  },
  "explanation": [
    "Stream events into Kafka; workers keep per-window counts (or approximate ones with count-min sketch) and a heap of the current top K.",
    "Publish the computed top-K list to a cache: millions of readers hit one small, hot key.",
    "Exact counts can be reconciled later in a batch job; trending only needs to be roughly right, quickly."
  ]
